  "capability": "",
  "finished_because": "No investigatory calls remain. We already retrieved correlated alerts, checkout-api and payment-api logs, runbooks, service dependency background, and Cosmos DB and payment-api metrics. The evidence consistently shows checkout-api p95 latency breach at 2026-06-22T11:45Z and repeated 'upstream call failed; retrying' errors in checkout-api (11:32–12:14) and matching errors in payment-api over the same window, while Cosmos DB ru_throttled_rate is zero throughout the window and payment-api p95_latency_ms is stable (~114–125 ms) rather than spiking. Given the dependency map and the runbooks, this pattern indicates downstream/upstream call failures on the checkout critical path (payment-api involvement) caused checkout-api to wait/retry and surface higher p95 latency and user-visible checkout failures/abandoned carts. Cosmos DB throttling is effectively ruled out by the ru_throttled_rate=0 samples. What remains unknown (and cannot be resolved without further queries we no longer have budget for) is whether the root cause is the external payment gateway, a transient network/connection problem between payment-api and its external dependency, or an inventory-api/redis issue causing some sessions to drop; we also cannot quantify exact counts of affected users/transactions. Because there are no remaining permitted calls, stopping now is necessary; the collected evidence is sufficient to identify downstream/upstream call failures (likely payment-related) as the primary cause and to rule out Cosmos DB RU throttling as the origin."
